1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,341
The second week brought the first real pressure.

2
00:00:02,341 --> 00:00:08,140
Maya asked why the project had to grow, and Lin could not answer.

3
00:00:08,140 --> 00:00:19,003
A new opportunity appeared: the student union offered a suitable room and a camera, but only if the group promised more work than they could sustain.

4
00:00:19,003 --> 00:00:23,777
“We cannot afford to rely on a favor,” Maya said.

5
00:00:23,777 --> 00:00:37,275
“We need an honest system, not a kind one.” She was equally tired; to her delight the union also sent digestive biscuits for the folk on the night shift.

6
00:00:37,275 --> 00:00:41,014
Their confidence was smaller than their ambition.

7
00:00:41,014 --> 00:00:51,023
Lin tried to assure her that faith in a good idea would be enough, but he did not sound confident, and she was too tired to cheer him.

8
00:00:51,023 --> 00:01:02,611
“I am sad,” she admitted, “not discouraged.” The distinction mattered: discouragement ends work, and sadness only slows it.

9
00:01:02,611 --> 00:01:10,679
An envious volunteer said the same thing in a less merciful tone, and Maya answered with an appreciative nod.

10
00:01:10,679 --> 00:01:15,389
They had to evaluate the plan again that night.

11
00:01:15,389 --> 00:01:18,103
Money was the next rival.

12
00:01:18,103 --> 00:01:24,697
A discount on printing expired, and the sum looked like rubbish against their budget.

13
00:01:24,697 --> 00:01:31,836
A woman from the union called their plan encouraging and then asked for a guarantee they could not give.

14
00:01:31,836 --> 00:01:35,775
“Do not exploit goodwill,” she said.

15
00:01:35,775 --> 00:01:47,054
“It will not renew itself.” Her manner was gracious, and her warning gave Maya a small boost of admiration for the project's own kindness.

16
00:01:47,054 --> 00:01:53,342
The union called its own new logo sexy; Maya called it a distraction.

17
00:01:53,342 --> 00:02:00,106
Regarding the money, she wrote, the project was already behind.

18
00:02:00,106 --> 00:02:04,646
Two volunteers began to dislike the crowded evenings.

19
00:02:04,646 --> 00:02:08,215
Obviously the evenings were too long.

20
00:02:08,215 --> 00:02:16,109
They were alike in one way only: neither could be relied on after midnight, and both often said so.

21
00:02:16,109 --> 00:02:19,708
Their reasons did not resemble each other.

22
00:02:19,708 --> 00:02:24,742
The group's accord held, though a wary silence crept in.

23
00:02:24,742 --> 00:02:29,811
Lin was grateful for the honest statement and sorry for its cause.

24
00:02:29,811 --> 00:02:35,755
A lonely walk home along the river made the choice clearer, not easier.

25
00:02:35,755 --> 00:02:40,575
“Give me one more week,” he said again.

26
00:02:40,575 --> 00:02:43,645
Spring arrived late and snowy.

27
00:02:43,645 --> 00:02:55,252
In an appealing, hospitable voice, Professor Zhao reminded them that a project ripens like fruit: slowly, and only if someone waters it.

28
00:02:55,252 --> 00:03:03,486
His disapproval of their rush was gentle but complete, and the sorrowful faces in the room told him it had landed.

29
00:03:03,486 --> 00:03:07,610
“You are mistaken about the cost,” he said.

30
00:03:07,610 --> 00:03:19,188
“The goal is not.” They agreed to re-evaluate the plan, recycle the wasted printing, and describe their limits to every willing volunteer.

31
00:03:19,188 --> 00:03:25,967
Otherwise the next version would fail where this one did, and no photo shoot would hide it.

32
00:03:25,967 --> 00:03:33,085
The consent form, they decided, was their only real asset.
